<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-28">28 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Challenger breaks apart after launch</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Challenger broke apart 73 seconds after lift-off, killing its seven crew, including teacher Christa McAuliffe. A faulty seal in a booster rocket was to blame, and shuttle flights stopped for 32 months.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-20">20 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union launches the core of the Mir space station</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Mir's first module was launched from Baikonur. Expanded over ten years, the station hosted crews from many nations and was continuously occupied for almost a decade before its re-entry in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-25">25 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">People Power Revolution forces Marcos from the Philippines</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After days of peaceful mass protest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos">Ferdinand Marcos</a> fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corazon-aquino">Corazon Aquino</a> was sworn in as president. His two decades of rule had included years of martial law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-26">26 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Reactor explodes at the Chernobyl nuclear plant</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A safety test went wrong at reactor No. 4 in Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, causing an explosion and fire that spread radioactive fallout across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Over 100,000 people were evacuated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/chernobyl-disaster" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chernobyl-disaster.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/chernobyl-disaster">Chernobyl disaster</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Chernobyl disaster was the explosion and fire at reactor No. 4 of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in the Ukrainian SSR on 26 April 1986, the worst accident in the history of nuclear power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/doi-moi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/doi-moi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/doi-moi">Đổi Mới</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Đổi Mới ('renovation') is the programme of economic reform adopted by the Sixth Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam in December 1986.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/moiwana-massacre">Moiwana massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Moiwana massacre was the killing of at least 39 inhabitants of the Ndyuka Maroon village of Moiwana in eastern Suriname, most of them women and children, by soldiers of the National Army on 29 November 1986, during the interior war against the Jungle…</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sixth-national-congress-of-the-communist-party-of-vietnam">Sixth National Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sixth National Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam met in Hanoi from 15 to 18 December 1986 and elected Nguyen Van Linh as general secretary.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/waldheim-affair" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waldheim-affair.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/waldheim-affair">Waldheim affair</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Waldheim affair was a controversy over the wartime past of Kurt Waldheim, former Secretary-General of the United Nations, during his successful campaign for the Austrian presidency in 1986.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/australia-act-1986">Australia Act 1986</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Australia Act 1986 comprises matching laws of the Australian and British parliaments that took effect on 3 March 1986.</p></div></li></ol></section>
